<title>UK: UK output prices up 0.1% in May.</title>
<headline>UK output prices up 0.1% in May.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Office for National Statistics (ONS) released the following provisional data on UK input and output prices in May. (Prev data in brackets)</p>
<p> OUTPUT PRICES (unadj)	   MAY	 APRIL  (PREL APRIL)</p>
<p> Monthly change		    0.1	 0.2	   (0.2)</p>
<p> Yr/yr change			1.0	 0.8	   (0.8)</p>
<p> Index (base 1990)		 125.1     125.0     (125.0)</p>
<p>OUTPUT PRICES EX FOOD/DRINK/TOBACCO/PETROLEUM (unadj)</p>
<p> Monthly change		    unch	0.1	   (0.1)</p>
<p> Yr/yr change			0.5	 0.5	   (0.5)</p>
<p> Index (base 1990)		 120.7     120.7     (120.7)</p>
<p>OUTPUT PRICES EX-FOOD/DRINK/TOBACCO/PETROLEUM (adj)</p>
<p> Monthly change		    0.1	 0.1	   (0.1)</p>
<p> Yr/yr change			0.6	 0.5	   (0.5)</p>
<p> Qtr/qtr change		    0.2	 0.1	   (0.1)</p>
<p> Qtr/qtr annual rate	     0.8	 0.3	   (0.3)</p>
<p> Index (base 1990)		 120.5     120.4     (120.4)</p>
<p>INPUT PRICES (MATERIALS AND FUEL) (unadj)</p>
<p> Monthly change		    0.7	-2.3	  (-2.1)</p>
<p> Yr/yr change		     -9.1	-10.8	(-10.5)</p>
<p> Index (base 1990)		 104.7     104.0     (104.0)</p>
<p>INPUT PRICES (MATERIALS AND FUEL) (adj)</p>
<p> Monthly change		    0.6	 -2.1	 (-1.9)</p>
<p> Yr/yr change		     -9.1	-10.7	(-10.5)</p>
<p> Index				 104.4     103.8     (104.0)</p>
<p>INPUT PRICES EX F, D, T, P (unadj)</p>
<p> Monthly change		    -0.1	-1.4	 (-1.4)</p>
<p> Yr/yr change			-7.7	-8.3	 (-8.2)</p>
<p> Index				 102.0	102.1    (102.2)</p>
<p>INPUT PRICES EX F, D, T, P (adj)</p>
<p> Monthly change		    unch	-1.2	 (-1.2)</p>
<p> Yr/yr change			-7.7	-8.1	 (-8.2)</p>
<p> Index				 102.6	102.6    (102.5)</p>
<p> INPUT COMPONENTS PCT CHANGE   MAY M/M		 MAY Y/Y</p>
<p> Fuel				  -1.5		     -5.2</p>
<p> Crude oil etc			6.5		    -11.6</p>
<p> Food (home produced)	     1.6		    -11.7</p>
<p> Food (imported)		    0.5		     -6.0</p>
<p> Other home produced		0.2		     -0.3</p>
<p> Metals				 0.5		    -10.2</p>
<p> Chemicals			   -0.3		     -9.6</p>
<p> Other imported materials	-0.1		     -8.8</p>
<p>Consensus of economists forecasts was for input prices to rise a seasonally adjusted 0.6 percent in May but fall 8.6 percent year-on-year. Unadjusted output prices are forecast flat and 1.0 percent higher year-on-year.</p>
<p>The main upward push in output prices came from petrol, the ONS said.</p>
